# Planetarium of Wan Shi Tong with an empty library: the scry is still a scry, and "whenever you scry" triggers once it is
# done "even if some or all of those actions were impossible" (CR 701.22d). Bot1's deck is its opening hand and nothing
# else. Bot1 puts the Planetarium out on turn 1 (Sol Ring, Black Lotus, Mox Jet) and activates it with Mox Pearl: the
# scry 2 looks at nothing (`! Bot1.Arrange`), the ability triggers all the same (`Stack.Count = 1`), and as it resolves
# there is no top card to look at or cast (`! Bot1.Accept`, `Bot1.Looked` absent).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Sol Ring
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Planetarium of Wan Shi Tong
Island

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Planetarium of Wan Shi Tong.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Planetarium of Wan Shi Tong.Activate
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Arrange
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 0
Bot1.Looked = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Planetarium of Wan Shi Tong.Tapped = true
Bot1.Hand = Island
